course: dictionary
lesson: 781
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Beaver» can name an animal, and it can also be an action word: to beaver away means to work very hard and steadily at something. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Beavers build dams of sticks, stones and mud» is about an animal, because animals build dams and live near water. But in «Dad will beaver away at his homework all evening», beaver is something you do, so it means working hard.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. "Dad will animal away at his homework" makes no sense, but "Dad will work hard at his homework" does, so the action meaning is right.
fact: A beaver is a large rodent with thick brown fur, strong teeth and a wide, flat tail.
fact: Beavers live near rivers and lakes.
fact: Beavers cut down trees with their teeth and build dams of sticks, stones and mud.
fact: «To beaver away» is informal and means to work very hard and steadily at something.
fact: The beaver is the national animal of Canada, and it appears on the Canadian five-cent coin.
exercise: In «Beavers build dams that make ponds where many other animals live», what is a beaver? | A type of tree | *An animal that builds dams and lives near water | A kind of stone | A person who works very hard
exercise: «Dad said he would beaver away at his maths homework all evening.» What does beaver away mean? | To swim across a river | To chew through wood | To sleep very late | *To work very hard and steadily
exercise: In «Beavers build dams that make ponds where many other animals live», which word names something beavers make across a stream? | pond | live | *dam | animals
test: Which country has the beaver as its national animal? | Britain | Australia | France | *Canada
test: Nadia says, «The beaver is an eager beaver for the new project.» What does eager beaver mean? | A beaver living in a lake | A beaver that is hungry | A person who is tired | *A very keen person
exam: Which meaning of beaver fits «Mum beavers away in the garden every Saturday, weeding and digging»? | A wide, flat tail | *To work hard and steadily | An animal with thick brown fur | A place near a river
